    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country E.164 national-number length validation in the owner create/update flow.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\nAfter a telephone is normalized to E.164 form (and the general \"8\u201315 digits\" check passes), `normalizeTelephone` now calls a new `validateNationalNumberLength` helper. It uses a `COUNTRY_NATIONAL_LENGTHS` map (`\"61\" \u2192 9`, `\"1\" \u2192 10`), selects the **longest** configured dialling code that prefixes the number, and rejects with **400 Bad Request** when the national-digit count doesn't match (e.g. `+61` with anything other than 9 national digits). Country codes with no configured rule remain permissive (only the existing 8\u201315 digit rule applies).\n\nBecause `normalizeTelephone` is the single choke point for both create and update, and `toComparableTelephone` already swallows its exceptions, legacy/seed telephones used only for duplicate comparison are unaffected.\n\n**Verification**: `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (`+61 123` \u2192 400) passes, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nNote: the acceptance case `+61 123` would already have been rejected by the pre-existing 8\u201315-digit rule (it's only 5 digits), but the new rule now enforces the actual per-country requirement the spec describes \u2014 e.g. a full-length but wrong-national-length number like `+61 1234 5678` (8 national digits) is now correctly rejected, whereas before it passed.",
