    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the existing structure of this controller cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit.** `OwnerRestControllerV1` already owns a family of private static telephone/email/address helpers (`normalizeTelephone`, `toComparableTelephone`, email validation, etc.). Adding `validateNationalNumberLength` as a sibling helper and calling it from within `normalizeTelephone` \u2014 right after the general 8\u201315 digit gate \u2014 places the new rule exactly where the existing normalization flow lives. It's a focused, single-responsibility extraction rather than inline bloat.\n- **Constant placement matches the file's idiom.** This class consistently co-locates each `private static final` constant next to the helper that consumes it (`CITY_CAPACITY`, `EMAIL_PATTERN` beside email validation, `ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS`). Declaring `COUNTRY_NATIONAL_LENGTHS` immediately above `validateNationalNumberLength` follows that established pattern, so a maintainer would find it where they'd expect.\n- **No duplication.** `normalizeTelephone`/E.164 logic exists only in the V1 owner controller \u2014 the V2 controller doesn't carry a parallel copy \u2014 so there's no shared unit this logic should have been hoisted into.\n- **Documentation stays coherent.** The Javadoc on `normalizeTelephone`, the new constant, and the new method are additive and consistent in tone/detail with the surrounding docs, and the `@throws` clause was updated to reflect the added rejection path.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
